Falsifies `paging::nth_allocation::a_failed_domain_build_maps_a_prefix`.

The defect: a "best effort" `build_identity_domain`. A page whose tables cannot be allocated is
skipped, the rest of the grant is mapped, and the first error is returned at the end. The kernel
caller `expect`s the build today, but any caller that unwinds by count would leave the pages past the
gap device-reachable.

Expected to fail: assertion (2), "what is left mapped is not a prefix of the request", at
`build_identity_domain` with allocation 0 failed.

`script/falsifications --sweep paging` replays it, weekly and per pull request, since milestone
742 (every test is falsified as routine). By hand, the same thing is:

    git apply crates/paging/falsifications/nth_allocation.a_failed_domain_build_maps_a_prefix.patch
    cargo test -p paging --test nth_allocation a_failed_domain_build_maps_a_prefix        # must fail
    git apply -R crates/paging/falsifications/nth_allocation.a_failed_domain_build_maps_a_prefix.patch

Run on 2026-10-04 (UTC), patagonia: red as predicted, green again after the revert.

